        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Iran positively reviewing Pakistan’s request for a two-week ceasefire, source says Middle East Issued on: 07/04/2026 - 22:14 Modified: 07/04/2026 - 22:16 U.S. President Donald Trump is aware ​of ‌Pakistan's ⁠proposal for a ‌two-week extension to a ⁠deadline he imposed on Iran, ​and a ‌response will come, White House press ‌secretary Karoline Leavitt ​said on Tuesday. \"The President has been ​made aware ​of the ​proposal, and a response ​will come,\" Leavitt said in a statement. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington. Trump's 'rhetoric itself could create a norm' for others to terrorise entire populations 07/04/2026 Middle East An 'eerie still' in Tehran amid Trump's apocalyptic threats 07/04/2026 Middle East Trump warns a 'whole civilization will die tonight' if a deal with Iran isn't reached 07/04/2026 Middle East Shootout outside Israeli consulate in Istanbul 07/04/2026 Middle East Trump threatens to take out Iran in 'one night' as deadline looms 07/04/2026 Middle East Trump says Iran could be 'taken out' on Tuesday 06/04/2026 Middle East Lebanon says Israeli strikes hit south Beirut, country's south 06/04/2026 Middle East Donald Trump issues expletive threat to Iran over Hormuz Strait blockage 06/04/2026 Middle East Egypt: Wide-ranging energy effects of the war in the Gulf ‌region 06/04/2026 Middle East"
